From: pdx203 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: ring: GPU timeline of each user submission

A6XX user submissions get a CP_EVENT_WRITE RB_DONE_TS with TIMESTAMP (the always-on counter, 19.2 MHz)
after the prologue and before the fence, into a 64-slot table at +1024 of the fence page. When a wait
first sees a fence, the GPU time between the stamps, the host time from the WPTR write and the GPU's
idle time before the submission are summed into native_adreno_ring_timeline, which the board prints
(pdx203 GpuProbe.cpp GPUTL row). It showed the home-screen frame's submission busy 11.7 ms on the GPU
around a 2.7 ms render pass (row-by-row shadow copies, fixed in the Metal frontend).

